1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,359
Last time, the CECL Genie showed us the four parts of a

2
00:00:04,379 --> 00:00:07,885
full answer: Choice, Evidence, Concept and Link.

3
00:00:11,872 --> 00:00:14,202
A little ant is hiding in this video.

4
00:00:14,452 --> 00:00:15,692
Can you spot it?

5
00:00:15,967 --> 00:00:17,807
Lock in first with your fingers.

6
00:00:18,077 --> 00:00:19,907
One finger for every point.

7
00:00:20,569 --> 00:00:21,719
Today you'll learn:

8
00:00:21,916 --> 00:00:23,656
Choice: only when you must pick.

9
00:00:23,931 --> 00:00:25,701
The Link: answer what was asked.

10
00:00:25,978 --> 00:00:27,208
Try it yourself.

11
00:00:27,863 --> 00:00:28,923
Question one.

12
00:00:29,203 --> 00:00:33,533
Ali wants to find out if more batteries make an electromagnet stronger.

13
00:00:33,813 --> 00:00:37,133
Set-up A has an iron nail, ten turns of wire and one

14
00:00:37,153 --> 00:00:37,883
battery.

15
00:00:38,153 --> 00:00:41,683
Set-up B has a steel nail, twenty turns of wire and two

16
00:00:41,703 --> 00:00:42,573
batteries.

17
00:00:42,853 --> 00:00:46,213
Explain why Ali's experiment is not a fair test.

18
00:00:47,932 --> 00:00:48,812
Round one.

19
00:00:49,102 --> 00:00:50,922
Does this answer need a Choice?

20
00:00:51,252 --> 00:00:52,292
One, yes.

21
00:00:52,572 --> 00:00:53,422
Two, no.

22
00:00:53,722 --> 00:00:55,072
Show me your fingers.

23
00:01:00,597 --> 00:01:01,577
Locked in!

24
00:01:01,855 --> 00:01:04,985
One. Every answer starts with a Choice!

25
00:01:05,337 --> 00:01:05,977
Two!

26
00:01:06,117 --> 00:01:07,807
The question says explain.

27
00:01:07,857 --> 00:01:09,387
There is nothing to pick.

28
00:01:09,738 --> 00:01:10,508
Two.

29
00:01:10,598 --> 00:01:14,268
A Choice is only for questions like which, or do you agree.

30
00:01:14,843 --> 00:01:16,153
The answer is two!

31
00:01:16,413 --> 00:01:17,993
Did you show two fingers?

32
00:01:18,263 --> 00:01:19,673
Put one finger up!

33
00:01:19,953 --> 00:01:22,763
A choice is the answer you pick when the question asks you

34
00:01:22,783 --> 00:01:26,613
to pick, such as: yes, I agree, or bar X!

35
00:01:27,341 --> 00:01:28,881
So where do we start?

36
00:01:29,752 --> 00:01:30,902
Look closer.

37
00:01:31,492 --> 00:01:33,042
Start with the Evidence.

38
00:01:33,622 --> 00:01:35,052
What did Ali change?

39
00:01:35,632 --> 00:01:36,692
Your turn.

40
00:01:41,249 --> 00:01:44,859
Ali changed the type of nail, the number of turns of wire,

41
00:01:44,879 --> 00:01:46,699
and the number of batteries.

42
00:01:47,059 --> 00:01:49,929
Now the Concept, the rule for a fair test.

43
00:01:49,998 --> 00:01:53,258
In a fair test, only one variable is changed.

44
00:01:53,838 --> 00:01:56,198
The other variables are kept the same.

45
00:01:56,553 --> 00:01:57,523
And the Link.

46
00:01:58,153 --> 00:01:59,203
Your turn.

47
00:02:03,764 --> 00:02:07,504
Thus, Ali cannot be sure that the number of batteries made the

48
00:02:07,524 --> 00:02:09,264
electromagnet stronger.

49
00:02:12,348 --> 00:02:13,578
Say it with me!

50
00:02:14,287 --> 00:02:17,287
Give a Choice only when the question asks you to pick.

51
00:02:20,808 --> 00:02:21,839
Question two.

52
00:02:21,859 --> 00:02:26,305
Siti says that a cockroach has the same life cycle as a

53
00:02:26,325 --> 00:02:27,093
butterfly.

54
00:02:27,113 --> 00:02:28,209
Do you agree?

55
00:02:28,229 --> 00:02:29,038
Explain.

56
00:02:29,761 --> 00:02:30,661
Showdown!

57
00:02:30,971 --> 00:02:32,101
Double points.

58
00:02:32,371 --> 00:02:34,881
Basil's answer is missing one part.

59
00:02:35,161 --> 00:02:36,071
Which one?

60
00:02:36,361 --> 00:02:37,941
One, two, three, or four?

61
00:02:44,450 --> 00:02:45,430
Locked in!

62
00:02:45,708 --> 00:02:50,248
Four! Basil never says what the question asked: is it the same life

63
00:02:50,268 --> 00:02:51,138
cycle?

64
00:02:53,716 --> 00:02:54,826
Four fingers?

65
00:02:55,096 --> 00:02:57,006
Put up two more on your score hand!

66
00:02:57,503 --> 00:02:58,473
Be the Link!

67
00:02:58,753 --> 00:02:59,743
Shrink down.

68
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:00,953
Quietly.

69
00:03:03,235 --> 00:03:05,215
You are a short green sentence.

70
00:03:05,995 --> 00:03:08,115
On one side, the science rule.

71
00:03:08,905 --> 00:03:10,765
On the other side, the question.

72
00:03:11,358 --> 00:03:13,778
You stretch out, and join them together.

73
00:03:14,548 --> 00:03:18,438
Thus, the cockroach and the butterfly do not have the same life

74
00:03:18,458 --> 00:03:19,218
cycle.

75
00:03:19,811 --> 00:03:20,571
Click!

76
00:03:21,391 --> 00:03:22,811
The answer is whole.

77
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:27,150
Here is my answer to the fridge question.

78
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:29,140
Magnets attract steel.

79
00:03:30,015 --> 00:03:31,165
Look closer.

80
00:03:31,765 --> 00:03:35,285
Explain why the door of a refrigerator stays closed.

81
00:03:35,875 --> 00:03:37,695
Pip wrote a true Concept.

82
00:03:38,255 --> 00:03:39,955
But it is only one part.

83
00:03:40,525 --> 00:03:42,955
Your turn: what does the question show?

84
00:03:43,525 --> 00:03:44,995
And what does it ask?

85
00:03:49,555 --> 00:03:52,855
Evidence: there is a strip of magnet inside the edge of the

86
00:03:52,875 --> 00:03:56,845
door, and the body of the refrigerator is made of steel.

87
00:03:57,206 --> 00:04:01,606
Link: Thus, the magnetic strip is attracted to the steel body, and

88
00:04:01,626 --> 00:04:03,296
this keeps the door closed.

89
00:04:03,657 --> 00:04:06,677
A link is the sentence that joins the science rule to what

90
00:04:06,697 --> 00:04:11,167
the question asks, such as: thus, this keeps the door closed!

91
00:04:11,822 --> 00:04:14,512
If you help with one thing, help with the Link.

92
00:04:17,508 --> 00:04:18,798
Say it with me!

93
00:04:19,506 --> 00:04:22,426
The Link joins the rule to what the question asks.

94
00:04:22,936 --> 00:04:24,756
It often starts with Thus.

95
00:04:27,518 --> 00:04:28,623
Say it with us!

96
00:04:29,283 --> 00:04:30,151
Choice?

97
00:04:30,863 --> 00:04:32,140
Only if you pick!

98
00:04:35,683 --> 00:04:36,608
Evidence?

99
00:04:37,263 --> 00:04:38,430
From the question!

100
00:04:42,083 --> 00:04:43,074
Concept?

101
00:04:43,663 --> 00:04:44,830
The rule I know!

102
00:04:49,338 --> 00:04:50,798
Show me your score hand!

103
00:04:51,078 --> 00:04:52,528
Two fingers or more?

104
00:04:52,818 --> 00:04:54,178
You beat the Buddies.

105
00:04:54,468 --> 00:04:55,538
Three fingers?

106
00:04:55,818 --> 00:04:56,818
High five!

107
00:04:57,246 --> 00:04:58,646
Did you spot the ant?

108
00:04:58,916 --> 00:05:00,456
It was on the window ledge!

109
00:05:00,744 --> 00:05:02,334
Here is a fun fact!

110
00:05:02,534 --> 00:05:05,754
An ant leaves a smell trail from the food to its nest,

111
00:05:05,774 --> 00:05:07,394
and the other ants follow it.

112
00:05:07,514 --> 00:05:08,824
It is a link!

113
00:05:09,026 --> 00:05:10,306
Tell someone at home!

114
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:15,242
You can learn the CECL way with the Genie in TheOneApp.

115
00:05:15,262 --> 00:05:19,184
Open TheOneApp, tap Questions, then the CECL Genie.

116
00:05:19,204 --> 00:05:21,392
The Genie is for members.

117
00:05:21,866 --> 00:05:27,126
CECL means Choice, Evidence, Concept and Link, such as Momo's full answer

118
00:05:27,146 --> 00:05:28,341
about bar X!

119
00:05:29,303 --> 00:05:31,503
Let's read today's key words together!

120
00:05:31,793 --> 00:05:32,553
Ready?

121
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:33,680
Choice.

122
00:05:35,107 --> 00:05:35,867
Link.

123
00:05:37,255 --> 00:05:38,424
CECL.

124
00:05:40,448 --> 00:05:41,388
Well done!

125
00:05:42,370 --> 00:05:43,471
Say it with us!

126
00:05:44,272 --> 00:05:45,022
Ready?

127
00:05:45,145 --> 00:05:45,805
One!

128
00:05:46,145 --> 00:05:46,845
two!

129
00:05:47,150 --> 00:05:48,325
Now you know!
